    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One more thing though—we've had issues in a previous project where the floor looked fine initially but then seemed to develop these weird, tiny, irregular pits or marks that didn't seem to come from standard cleaning or walking. Is that something that can happen with the sealer wearing down, or is it just the material itself failing over time?",
